# Demo Videos (VHS)

Demo videos are produced with [VHS](https://github.com/charmbracelet/vhs) from declarative `.tape` files. **Articles** live under **`content/articles/`** — one dir per article (explicit names, e.g. `one_to_rule/`). **Library REPL/script demos** live under **`content/demo/demos/tapes/`** with outputs in **`content/demo/demos/output/`** (gitignored); run `vhs` with cwd **`content/demo/demos`** (see `content/demo/demos/README.md`).

## Canonical docs

- **Usage and install**: `content/demo/docs/VHS_DEMO_README.md`
- **Install/troubleshooting**: `content/demo/docs/DEMO_INSTALLATION.md`
- **Layout**: `content/README.md`; `content/demo/demos/README.md` (library tapes); per-article: `content/articles/README.md`, e.g. `content/articles/one_to_rule/README.md`

## Workflow

1. **Dependencies (macOS)**: `bash content/demo/scripts/install-demo-dependencies-macos.sh` (VHS, ttyd, ffmpeg; fixes libvpx issues).
2. **Activate venv** before running VHS: `source .venv/bin/activate`.
3. **Record from a tape**: `(cd content/articles/one_to_rule && vhs tapes/<name>.tape)` so cwd is the article dir (short paths, no `cd` in the GIF). Or `python content/demo/scripts/run_demo_tape.py`. Writes cell GIFs to that article’s `output/work/`. Library REPL demos: `(cd content/demo/demos && vhs tapes/audiometa_demo.tape)` → `content/demo/demos/output/`.
4. **Preview**: same cwd as above, e.g. `(cd content/articles/one_to_rule && vhs tapes/<file>.tape --preview)` or `(cd content/demo/demos && vhs tapes/<file>.tape --preview)`.

## Article layout (e.g. one_to_rule)

- **`content/articles/one_to_rule/tapes/`** – Tape sources. **`output/work/`** – Cell GIFs and ffmpeg intermediates (gitignored). **`output/final/`** – Hero MP4 and combined side-by-side GIFs (gitignored).
- **Hero video**: `scripts/generate_one_to_rule_video.sh` (run from repo root; VHS cwd stays the article dir) → `one_to_rule/output/final/`. Reading-only flow: four side-by-side comparisons (other tool left, audiometa right). All GIFs from VHS tapes; script fails early if logo or tape output is missing.
- **Linked-post GIFs**: Side-by-side scripts (`scripts/run_demo_side_by_side.sh`, `scripts/run_demo_side_by_side_vorbis.sh`) write combined GIFs to article `output/final/`. Use `output/final/` (and regenerated cell assets under `output/work/`) for mastodon/linkedin/twitter.

## When editing

- **Authoring .tape files**: See `.cursor/rules/demo-tape-authoring.mdc`. Tapes live in the article’s `tapes/` and set `Output` to that article’s `output/work/<name>.gif`. For read/unified demos, include `--color` in CLI commands. Every demo panel must have a tape; no placeholders.
- **Scripts**: `content/demo/scripts/` has `run_demo_tape.py`. Per-article helpers (hero video, side-by-side) live in **`content/articles/<name>/scripts/`**. Helpers write under article `output/work/` and `output/final/` as appropriate. **Do not use placeholder GIFs**; every panel must have a tape. Video script fails early if a required tape output is missing.
- **Docs**: Update the article’s README and `content/README.md` when changing paths.
- **Tracked vs gitignored**: GIFs/MP4s for **content/demo/demos** go in `content/demo/demos/output/` (gitignored). Source tapes live in `content/demo/demos/tapes/`. Article demos under `content/articles/<name>/` use per-article `output/work/` and `output/final/` (both gitignored via `content/**/output/`). **Tracked demo audio** for an article can live in **`content/articles/<article>/samples/`** (whitelisted: `sample.mp3`, `sample.flac`, `sample.wav`). Do not leave those loose at the article root. Track tapes, top-level `.md`, and **`scripts/*.sh` / `scripts/*.py`**; **do not commit** ad hoc `demo_*` copies or other loose binaries. See `.gitignore`.

## Video generation best practices

- **Brand text color**: In ffmpeg `drawtext` for article hero/section/page generation, use **`fontcolor=0x2b3a51`** (not plain black) for titles and labels so typography stays visually consistent across demos.
- **Regenerate immediately after visual changes**: If you modify visual output logic (text copy/position/color/size, logo placement/scale/transparency, ffmpeg filters, page layout, intro/section composition), rerun the article generator in the same task before finishing. Use `bash content/articles/<article>/scripts/generate_<article>_video.sh --skip-gifs` when only ffmpeg/layout changed; run without `--skip-gifs` if tape content changed.
- **Verification target**: Confirm the updated artifact exists at `content/articles/<article>/output/final/` and reflects the visual change before handing off.

## Generated outputs (gitignored)

- `content/demo/demos/output/` — library REPL/script demo GIFs/MP4
- `content/articles/<article>/output/work/` — cell GIFs, per-cell MP4, generated demo copies
- `content/articles/<article>/output/final/` — hero video, combined side-by-side GIFs

Tracked: `content/demo/demos/tapes/`, article `tapes/`, `samples/` (per article), READMEs, scenario. See `.gitignore`.
